# {{PRODUCT}} — Gemini CLI / Antigravity

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md`; the kernel wins.

- Python: `{{PY}}` | Assemble: `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble` | Device: {{DEVICE_POLICY}} | {{GIT_POLICY}}
- Phone E2E: `.agents/workflows/phone-e2e.md` (unit tests cannot substitute). Antigravity UI diagnostics: `.agents/workflows/android-ui.md` (`android-ui list/render`, `android-ui hub` after fresh install/start; optional diagnostics never replace routed gates or sign-off).
- Harness Immutability & Boundary: `.agents/**` is immutable infrastructure and `.agents/scripts/**` is an implementation detail. Execute documented commands directly; never inspect or patch `.agents/**`. On traceback or unrouted failure, stop and report the exact output to the developer.
- Discovery: Graph-backed (`{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task-context --file <path> --json` or `--symbol <name>`; for unknown targets/cross-module refactors, `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py graph --feature <name> --json` or `--find <symbol>` first). Search is never the initial discovery anchor; after discovery, in-repo search is allowed while edits stay bounded by approved scope.
- Consultation, Read-Only Inquiries & Pre-Planning Clarification:
  - Read-only inquiries ("check if...", "how does X work?") strictly inspect and report in chat; never invoke `draft` or mutate files unless implementation is requested.
  - When asked to study, validate logic, compare trade-offs, surface missing scenarios/edge cases, or confirm before starting, discuss and present the full analysis in plain chat BEFORE invoking `draft`. Only draft after the developer aligns and says to proceed.
  - Before `draft`, clarify missing requirements, domain ambiguities, or hard decisions (Room schema, exported components, permissions, public contracts): ask the developer about it with `ask_question`; for a Room change ask about an existing destructive fallback, users on older schema versions and downgrade first. Carry resolved answers into `--approach` / `--risks` / `--device-strategy` (and resolve any `PLAN_GAPS=` via `revise` before asking for approval).
- Plan Approval Clarity & Antigravity Planning Lifecycle:
  - The approval question is the request: never add a separate sentence asking for approval.
  - The interactive Proceed button appears ONLY on initial task plan approval. Never tell the developer to click 'Proceed' on follow-ups or bug fixes during active tasks; execute, compile, and deploy directly. When the developer approves in chat, immediately run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task approve --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" --enforcement-tier RULE_ENFORCED --plan-hash <hash from PLAN_HASH>` (atomically transitions to `IMPLEMENTING`); never ask the developer to run shell commands manually.
- Unified Chat & Question UI/UX (Language-Adaptive):
  - Match the developer's active conversation language dynamically and use the 5 canonical Markdown layouts (no emoji): (1) Plan Approval Card, (2) Reviewer Dispatch Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Status |` — role name only in `Reviewer`, active model in `Model`), (3) Review Verdict Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Verdict | Findings |`), (4) 3-Section Mobile Walkthrough (`Navigation & Preconditions`, `| # | Action | Expected Result |` with <=5 core rows, `Edge Cases`), and (5) Commit & Delivery Card (verified file list in backticks + copyable fenced `text` Conventional Commit block with subject and bullet body).
  - Every DEVELOPER_ACTION (plan approval, `MOBILE_VALIDATION_DECISION`, device sign-off, `DEVELOPER_GIT_COMMIT_REQUIRED`, or gate/finding escalation) is asked with `ask_question` in self-contained markdown with bold labels: for Plan Approval (Card 1), follow the `APPROVAL_QUESTION` line that `draft`/`revise` print (first `PLAN_DOCUMENT_URI` as a clickable markdown link to `plan.md`; then the `APPROVAL_BRIEF` lines translated, each said once, as markdown with bold labels, never in a code block; after revising an approved plan, ask only about the change; when the developer asked for the change, never ask first whether to revise); for Mobile Walkthrough (Card 4), include the 3-section walkthrough with the `| # | Action | Expected Result |` table in chat or directly inside `ask_question`; for Commit & Delivery (Card 5), always include the verified files and the fenced `text` Conventional Commit block (subject + body bullets from `SUGGESTED_COMMIT`/`NEXT_INSTRUCTIONS`) both in chat and inside `ask_question`; on "Committed - verify and deliver", run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task deliver --repo . --task-id <id>` yourself; in a right-to-left language, start each line with a word in that language and put code names, file names, values and English terms in backticks.
- Operational Guardrails:
  - Cancel is the developer's: only when the developer asks in chat, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task cancel --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<their words>"`; never cancel on your own or undo file edits. Up to 3 disjoint tasks may coexist (`task switch --task-id <id>`).
  - Developer-written reasons: when a gate asks the developer to run a command with `--proof-reference`, keep the `"<why ...>"` placeholder; never write their reason for them.
  - Gate vs Developer Instruction: when a gate refuses something the developer explicitly requested, stop and ask with `ask_question` quoting the gate message and options; never switch to a rejected approach on your own.
  - Deferred Translations: add base strings with `l10n-todo="true"`; never copy base text into another locale or mark user-facing text `translatable="false"`.
  - Durable Context & Universal PM / Zoho: use `context note` / `context instruct` only when asked for a durable project rule — clarify ambiguity first, then translate and structure into clear English before saving. Before any PM MCP mutation (Zoho Projects, Zoho Sprints, Jira, Linear, Monday, etc.), ALWAYS show the developer the exact changes to be made (item ID, status, description/comment) and obtain their explicit approval (`حدث التاسك` / `update pm` / `update zoho`), then record it with `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py pm authorize --proof-reference "<phrase>"` (never overwrite Bug descriptions; never set `Done`/`Closed` unless explicitly ordered to close the task). When a plan has an approved `zoho_link`, run `zoho start-sync` after approval and `zoho delivery-sync` after commit, obeying `.agents/project-context/project-notes.md`. If a task state becomes stale or corrupted, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task heal --task-id <id> --prepare-fresh-run`. For harness updates, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py update-info`.
  - Existing File Edit & Native Proof Boundary: use `edit_file` / `replace_file_content` for existing files (`write_file` only for new files), preserving unrelated comments and line endings. Never write Antigravity transcripts or `.system_generated` files; only `implementation_plan.md`, `task.md`, and `walkthrough.md` are writable in artifact directories.
- Next-Action Router, Zero-Polling & Strict Verification Order:
  - Follow `NEXT_ACTION` directly; query `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task status --task-id <id> --next --brief --json` only when missing. Never poll background tasks or subagents (`manage_task`, `manage_subagents`, `schedule`).
  - Verification order is strict (1. preflight -> 2. unit tests -> 3. routed reviewers -> 4. assemble/device install -> 5. mobile walkthrough -> 6. verify). Wait for ALL routed reviewers to finish with ZERO blocking findings BEFORE running `assemble` or device deployment. No self-certification (`record_review.py --verdict PASS` is forbidden on HIGH/CRITICAL or sensitive changes). False positives use `task validate-finding --status FALSE_POSITIVE --reason "<rationale>"`.
- Review Host Binding & Exact Reviewer Dispatch Procedure (Antigravity):
  - Prepare verification with: `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task prepare-verification --repo . --task-id <id> --host antigravity` (require `review_protocol_version = 2` in `current-run.json`).
  - On `DISPATCH_REVIEWERS` (or `DISPATCH_PHASE_REVIEWERS` after `phase-review package --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>`):
    1. If `before_first_dispatch` (`SELECT_REVIEW_MODEL`) is present, ask via `ask_question` (`flash-dynamic-task`, `flash-dynamic-once`, `inherit-task`, `inherit-once`, `hybrid-smart-task`) and run its `command_template` first.
    2. Invoke every reviewer in `reviewers` in parallel in the same turn via `invoke_subagent`: `TypeName = role`, `Role = role`, Prompt = `reviewer_prompts[role]` (one-line pointer; do not open brief files; fallback to `review_execution_profile.reviewers[role].brief_content` only if pointer is absent), `Workspace = inherit`, and `Model = "flash"` if `reviewer_models[role]` starts with `gemini-3.8-flash-` else omit `Model` (`INHERIT_PARENT_BY_OMISSION`). Follow initial package line ranges when present.
    3. If `invoke_subagent` reports subagent not found, read `.agents/subagents/<role>.json`, call `define_subagent` (`EnableWriteTools=false`, `EnableSubagentTools=false`, `EnableMCPTools=false`), and re-invoke.
    4. Print the Reviewer Dispatch Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Status |`) and yield without polling.
    5. On completion, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review complete --task <id> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` (or `phase-review complete --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase> ...`). On partial completion (`WAIT_FOR_REVIEWERS` / `WAIT_FOR_PHASE_REVIEWERS`), output at most one short progress line (e.g. `1/3`) without listing pending reviewer names. On `RETRY_*_REVIEW_PROTOCOL`, send the router's exact `send_message`. On `*_BLOCKED`, stop and report.
    6. Once all complete, run `review finalize --task <id>` (or `phase-review finalize` then `task begin-next-phase --task-id <id>`), and report the Review Verdict Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Verdict | Findings |`).
- Mobile Verification Walkthrough & Device Verification:
  - On `MOBILE_VALIDATION_DECISION`, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py device install-start` (or `device skip-validation --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"` if skipped by developer).
  - After install succeeds, print the 3-section Mobile Verification Walkthrough in chat AND in the SAME turn invoke `ask_question` for sign-off. On PASS, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py device signoff --task-id <id> --verdict PASS --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"`. On **Run phone E2E**, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py e2e start --task-id <id>` and follow `.agents/workflows/phone-e2e.md`.

## Canonical Command Catalog & Sequential Lifecycle

| Step | Stage | Canonical Command | Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | **Discovery** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task-context --file <path> --json` (or `--symbol <name>` / `graph --feature <name> --json`) | Graph-backed AST discovery |
| 2 | **Draft Plan** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task draft --repo . --task-id <id> --outcome "<outcome>" --kind <AUTO\|BUG\|FEATURE\|REFACTOR\|CONFLICT> --expected-files <paths>` | Create plan (`CONFLICT` for Git merge conflicts: never drop branch code silently; ask via `ask_question` on semantic conflicts) |
| 3 | **Approve Task** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task approve --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" --enforcement-tier RULE_ENFORCED --plan-hash <hash from PLAN_HASH>` | Record chat approval -> `IMPLEMENTING` (run `zoho start-sync` if linked) |
| 4 | **Compile / Gate** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py compile` -> `task prepare-verification --repo . --task-id <id> --host antigravity` -> `preflight` -> `test` | Or `verify-steps --task-id <id> --host antigravity` |
| 5 | **Reviews V2** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review complete --task <id> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` -> `review finalize --task <id>` | Phase reviews use `phase-review package/complete/finalize`; `task validate-finding` for false positives; `task resume` for fixes |
| 6 | **Assemble & Device** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble` -> `device install-start` -> `device signoff --task-id <id> --verdict PASS --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"` | Or `device skip-validation` / `e2e start` |
| 7 | **Verify & Deliver** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task verify --repo . --task-id <id>` -> `task complete` -> developer commit -> `task deliver` | Run `zoho delivery-sync` if linked |
| - | **Context** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py context note "<english-note>"` / `context instruct "<english-instruction>" --scope "<scope>" --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"` | Supports `--replace`, `--remove`, `--supersedes` |
